Package: sparseGenSetCal
Type: Package
Title: Calibration for Sparse Gene-Set Scores
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ming", "Tang", role = "aut"),
    person("Xin", "Chen", role = "aut"),
    person("Qiwen", "Duan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "duanqiwen603@gmail.com"))
Description: Rank-based gene-set scores such as AUCell and UCell are sums over
    the top ranks of each cell.  In a shallow cell far fewer genes are detected
    than the rank ceiling admits, so the unused slots are filled by genes with a
    zero count, ordered by an arbitrary tie-break.  A gene that is never
    expressed therefore still contributes to the score, with a probability that
    depends on how many genes the cell detected, and sequencing depth tracks
    almost every biological axis of interest.  This package writes that
    contribution down in closed form, measures it in a given dataset before any
    association is tested, draws null gene sets matched to the observation on
    detection rate, expression and co-detection, and reports the false-positive
    rate of the cutpoint rules an analyst would otherwise apply without
    checking.  It is the companion package to the manuscript of the same name.
